# Patterns that must NEVER enter your dotfiles repo.
# This file is the single source of those patterns and is tracked in the repo.
# core.excludesFile in the yadm REPO config points at it, set by:
#     yadm gitconfig core.excludesFile ~/.config/omarchy-desktop/.gitignore
# import.sh sets it on every machine (step 5/6), export.sh before every commit.
#
# Do NOT set this with `yadm config core.excludesFile` - that writes yadm's own file
# (~/.config/yadm/config) which git does NOT read (yadm has no excludesFile handling and
# does not forward core.* to git). Verified A/B: a fresh *.lock file was not ignored, and
# after `yadm gitconfig` it is. Test with `yadm check-ignore --no-index -v <file>` on an
# UNTRACKED file - check-ignore prints nothing for already tracked files, so testing on
# those proves nothing.
# export.sh also has a guard that refuses to commit junk regardless of whether the git
# excludes work on a given machine.

*.lock
*.bak*
*.tmp
*.log

# local backup copies (working copies, they do not travel)
backups/

# local working notes (durable knowledge belongs in the tooling docs / INVENTORY.md)
SESSION-STATE.md
